.\" Manpage for dpino
.\" Generated for dpino v0.1.0
.TH DPINO 1 "December 2024" "v0.1.0" "dpino manual"
.SH NAME
dpino \- Rust-powered package metadata extractor + desktop entry generator + installer + browser
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dpino
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
.B dpino scan
[\fB\-\-path\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
.PP
.B dpino inspect
\fIPATH\fR
.PP
.B dpino list
[\fB\-\-json\fR]
.PP
.B dpino extract
\fIPATH\fR [\fB\-\-out\fR \fIDIR\fR]
.PP
.B dpino install-desktop
\fIPATH\fR [\fB\-\-user\fR] [\fB\-\-dry-run\fR]
.PP
.B dpino uninstall
\fIDESKTOP_ID\fR [\fB\-\-user\fR]
.PP
.B dpino refresh
.PP
.B dpino browse
[\fB\-\-path\fR \fIPATH\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dpino
is a comprehensive tool for managing Debian packages (.deb), AppImages (.AppImage), and AppDir packages. It can scan directories for packages, extract metadata, generate Freedesktop-compliant desktop entries, install them to XDG directories, and provide an interactive TUI browser for package management.
.PP
dpino supports three package formats:
.TP
.B Debian packages (.deb)
Extracts control.tar.* and data.tar.*, parses control files, extracts desktop entries and icons from packages, and auto-generates desktop entries if not present.
.TP
.B AppImage
Uses \fB\-\-appimage-extract\fR to extract contents, reads desktop entries from extracted squashfs-root, extracts icons, and wraps Exec line with absolute path to AppImage.
.TP
.B AppDir
Reads AppRun executable, reads included .desktop files, and extracts icons from usr/share/icons or local icons.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS scan
Scan a directory for packages and extract their metadata.
.TP
\fB\-\-path\fR, \fB\-p\fR \fIPATH\fR
Directory to scan for packages. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR, \fB\-j\fR
Output results as JSON instead of human-readable format.
.PP
Scans the specified directory recursively for .deb, .AppImage, and AppDir packages, extracts their metadata, and caches the results. The cache is stored in \fI~/.local/share/dpino/cache.json\fR.
.SS inspect
Inspect a single package file and display its metadata.
.TP
\fIPATH\fR
Path to the package file to inspect. Required.
.PP
Extracts and displays all metadata from the specified package file, including name, version, maintainer, description, categories, icon path, exec command, and mimetypes. Output is always in JSON format.
.SS list
List all packages that have been scanned and cached.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR, \fB\-j\fR
Output results as JSON instead of human-readable format.
.PP
Displays all packages that have been previously scanned and cached. The list includes package name, type, and source path.
.SS extract
Extract a package to a directory.
.TP
\fIPATH\fR
Path to the package file to extract. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-out\fR, \fB\-o\fR \fIDIR\fR
Output directory where the package will be extracted. Required.
.PP
Extracts the contents of the package to the specified directory. For .deb packages, extracts the data.tar.* contents. For AppImage, extracts the squashfs-root. For AppDir, copies the entire directory structure.
.SS install-desktop
Install a desktop entry and icon for a package.
.TP
\fIPATH\fR
Path to the package file to install. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fR, \fB\-u\fR
Install for current user (default: true). If false, installs system-wide (requires root).
.TP
\fB\-\-dry-run\fR
Perform a dry run without actually installing anything. Shows what would be installed.
.PP
Extracts metadata from the package, generates or uses the existing desktop entry, installs the desktop entry to \fI~/.local/share/applications\fR (or \fI/usr/share/applications\fR for system-wide), installs icons to \fI~/.local/share/icons\fR (or \fI/usr/share/icons\fR for system-wide), and refreshes the desktop database.
.SS uninstall
Uninstall a desktop entry.
.TP
\fIDESKTOP_ID\fR
Desktop entry ID to uninstall (e.g., "myapp.desktop"). Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fR, \fB\-u\fR
Uninstall from user directory (default: true). If false, uninstalls from system directory (requires root).
.PP
Removes the specified desktop entry file and refreshes the desktop database. The desktop entry ID should match the filename (e.g., "myapp.desktop").
.SS refresh
Refresh the desktop database and cache.
.PP
Updates the desktop database using \fBupdate-desktop-database\fR and refreshes the package cache. This ensures that newly installed desktop entries are recognized by the desktop environment.
.SS browse
Launch the interactive TUI browser.
.TP
\fB\-\-path\fR, \fB\-p\fR \fIPATH\fR
Optional directory to scan on startup before launching the TUI.
.PP
Launches a full-screen terminal user interface for browsing and managing packages. The TUI provides a package list, details view, and various actions.
.SH TUI KEYBINDINGS
When using the \fBbrowse\fR command, the following keybindings are available:
.TP
.B ↑/↓
Navigate up and down in the package list.
.TP
.B Enter
Inspect the selected package (shows detailed information).
.TP
.B i
Install desktop entry for the selected package.
.TP
.B e
Extract the selected package to /tmp/<package-name>.
.TP
.B d
Delete the selected package from the cache.
.TP
.B r
Refresh the package list.
.TP
.B q
Quit the TUI.
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
.B HOME
Used to determine the user's home directory for XDG data directories. Required.
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Controls logging verbosity. Set to "debug", "info", "warn", or "error". Default is "info".
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.local/share/dpino/cache.json\fR
Package metadata cache file.
.TP
\fI~/.local/share/applications/\fR
User desktop entries directory.
.TP
\fI~/.local/share/icons/\fR
User icons directory.
.TP
\fI/usr/share/applications/\fR
System desktop entries directory (requires root).
.TP
\fI/usr/share/icons/\fR
System icons directory (requires root).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Scan a directory for packages:
.RS
.B dpino scan --path /path/to/packages
.RE
.PP
Scan and output as JSON:
.RS
.B dpino scan --path /path/to/packages --json
.RE
.PP
Inspect a Debian package:
.RS
.B dpino inspect /path/to/package.deb
.RE
.PP
List all cached packages:
.RS
.B dpino list
.RE
.PP
Extract a package:
.RS
.B dpino extract /path/to/package.deb --out /tmp/extracted
.RE
.PP
Install desktop entry (dry run):
.RS
.B dpino install-desktop /path/to/package.deb --dry-run
.RE
.PP
Install desktop entry for current user:
.RS
.B dpino install-desktop /path/to/package.deb --user
.RE
.PP
Uninstall a desktop entry:
.RS
.B dpino uninstall myapp.desktop
.RE
.PP
Launch TUI browser:
.RS
.B dpino browse
.RE
.PP
Launch TUI browser and scan directory on startup:
.RS
.B dpino browse --path /path/to/packages
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
General error (invalid arguments, file not found, etc.)
.SH SECURITY
dpino follows security best practices:
.IP \(bu 4
All filenames are sanitized before use
.IP \(bu 4
No absolute path overwrites without explicit confirmation
.IP \(bu 4
Desktop entries and icons are only installed to XDG directories
.IP \(bu 4
Temporary directories are used for extraction
.IP \(bu 4
Extracted binaries are never executed
.PP
When installing system-wide (without \fB\-\-user\fR), root privileges are required. Always review packages before installation.
